<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila suzukii Turing onset wavelength at 2.046 µm (0 Ma, detail scale) (Drosophila suzukii)",
        "Drosophila suzukii Turing onset wavelength at 2.046 µm (0 Ma, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Drosophila suzukii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila suzukii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila suzukii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That D. takahashii has been measured at a 2.455 µm pigment wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: That subobscura, suzukii and takahashii form a stratigraphic ancestor chain. All three are extant (0 Ma).",
        "does_not_claim: That yellow or ebony enzyme kinetics are the Schnakenberg reactions.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.037, b=1.284, D_v/D_u=12.6, with D_u solved so lambda_c = 2.046 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Subobscura is the same diffusivities with a=0.52, b=0.18 so f_u = -17/35.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Takahashii is the same kinetics with diffusivities multiplied by 1.44, so lambda_c = 2.4552 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: A two-species reaction-diffusion system selects a finite onset wavenumber k_c (Turing 1952).",
        "reported_in_source: Male D. suzukii has an apical wing spot; the female has a serrated ovipositor (Atallah 2014).",
        "reported_in_source: Spot presence in the suzukii–biarmipes clade is a yellow cis-regulatory gain (Gompel 2005; Prud'homme 2006; Koshikawa 2020).",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2.046 µm value is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a published granule measurement.",
        "transfer_boundary: The McEvey plate anchors the animal and the wing-spot dimorphism. Its pixels are coarser than 2 µm." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila suzukii (Spotted-Wing Drosophila)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-suzukii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_suzukii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila suzukii; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Male D. suzukii has an apical wing spot; the female has a serrated ovipositor (Atallah 2014). | Spot presence in the suzukii–biarmipes clade is a yellow cis-regulatory gain (Gompel 2005; Prud'homme 2006; Koshikawa 2020). | A two-species reaction-diffusion system selects a finite onset wavenumber k_c (Turing 1952).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.037, b=1.284, D_v/D_u=12.6, with D_u solved so lambda_c = 2.046 µm. | Subobscura is the same diffusivities with a=0.52, b=0.18 so f_u = -17/35. | Takahashii is the same kinetics with diffusivities multiplied by 1.44, so lambda_c = 2.4552 µm.; transfer_boundary: The 2.046 µm value is the campaign detail-scale assignment, not a published granule measurement. | The McEvey plate anchors the animal and the wing-spot dimorphism. Its pixels are coarser than 2 µm.; does_not_claim: That yellow or ebony enzyme kinetics are the Schnakenberg reactions. | That D. takahashii has been measured at a 2.455 µm pigment wavelength. | That subobscura, suzukii and takahashii form a stratigraphic ancestor chain. All three are extant (0 Ma).]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
